WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.280
This chart plots Tasmania's financial
future.

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.960
If the state stays on its current
trajectory, independent economic

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.640
reviews project net debt will hit $16
billion by the

4
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.560
year 2034. To put that in perspective,
that's more than

5
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.920
a quarter of the entire state's economy,
leaving the government

6
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.400
borrowing money just to pay the interest
on its past

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.560
borrowing. Both the official liberal
budget and the Greens' alternative

8
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.880
budget identify this exact crisis,
starting from this identical financial

9
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.320
baseline. Despite totally opposite
political ideologies, both budgets project an

10
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.560
operating surplus by the exact same year,
2027.

11
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.520
The liberal government's path there relies
on a strategy of

12
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.640
subtraction. Their budget pulls $1.46
billion out of operational spending

13
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.320
over the next four years.

14
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.120
The Greens take a different route,
canceling all of those

15
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.680
spending cuts and instead introduce $930
million in new taxes

16
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.360
on specific industries.

17
00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.080
The technical question of balancing the
books has been solved.

18
00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.960
The political battle is now over who
carries the weight

19
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.240
of that repair.

20
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:08.680
Neither side is completely upfront about
the collateral damage of

21
00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.320
their plans. Let's look at the Liberal
government's $1.46 billion

22
00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.280
in planned operational efficiencies.

23
00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.720
The budget papers themselves note that
finding this much savings

24
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.800
is equivalent to cutting roughly 1,700
full-time roles.

25
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.640
The Department of Health alone is tasked
with absorbing $702

26
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.640
million of that total.

27
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.520
The government claims they can remove
hundreds of millions of

28
00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:36.760
dollars from the health system without
affecting frontline service delivery.

29
00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:40.440
However, the budget itself lists the
actual deliverability of these

30
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.440
savings as a formal risk.

31
00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.560
With health and education absorbing the
largest shares of these

32
00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.080
job losses, the impact is heaviest on
sectors where women

33
00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.360
make up the vast majority of the public
sector workforce.

34
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:55.440
These cuts are a direct result of a no-new
taxes

35
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.720
policy. By freezing the revenue side of
the ledger, the

36
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.560
government chooses to shield legacy
industries from contributing to the

37
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.560
repair. This model of fiscal repair
balances the books by

38
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.560
transferring the financial burden away
from corporate entities and onto

39
00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.040
public servants and the healthcare system.

40
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.400
The Greens' alternative budget reverses
this approach.

41
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.720
They plan to raise $930 million over four
years by

42
00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.720
expanding Tasmania's own source revenue,
which is currently among the

43
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.080
lowest in the country.

44
00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.440
There is no historical precedent for a
salmon royalty of

45
00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.200
this scale in Tasmania.

46
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.880
Booking the entire amount on an aggressive
timeline ignores the

47
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.000
reality that these industries will likely
tie these taxes up

48
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.440
in court for years.

49
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.680
While relying on corporate revenue
protects human services, it builds

50
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.080
the entire state budget on legally
untested, volatile income streams

51
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.160
that might never actually hit the state's
bank account.

52
00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.600
Both sides point to a recent independent
review by economist

53
00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.480
Saul Eslake to prove their math is right.

54
00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.880
But Eslake's report explicitly warned the
government against using efficiency

55
00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.640
dividends and vacancy controls, the exact
tools the liberals are

56
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.800
deploying. In fact, both Eslake and the
state treasury recommended

57
00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.440
broadening the state's own source tax
base.

58
00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:16.280
The independent economic consensus aligns
closer to the Greens' revenue

59
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.360
strategy than the government's cuts.

60
00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:21.960
However, the official budget contains a
significant omission.

61
00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:26.920
Look through the government's glossy
overview document, and the $567

62
00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.120
million Macquarie Point Stadium is
missing.

63
00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.480
It is listed only as a northern access
road.

64
00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.760
This chart shows the priorities they
aren't talking about.

65
00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:41.880
The budget finds $567 million for that
arena, while allocating

66
00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.720
just $11.4 million across its entire
women's and equity package.

67
00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.120
The Greens have their own honesty problem.

68
00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.920
Their headline claim that their plan
results in lower net

69
00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.480
debt than the official budget is false on
a key

70
00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.760
metric. This table from the Greens' budget
shows their general

71
00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:01.120
government sector net debt ends up $13
million higher than

72
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.960
the Liberals by 2030.

73
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.720
Down here in the 2029-30 column, the
official budget projects

74
00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:12.480
$9,466 million. The Greens' projection
hits $9,479

75
00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.600
million. Voters are choosing between a
government hiding its most

76
00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.800
expensive project from the public and an
opposition using accounting

77
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.440
technicalities to overclaim its financial
prudence.

78
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.440
The budget Tasmania actually needs is a
hybrid, hiding in

79
00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.520
the overlap of these two documents.

80
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.000
It would require the Greens' diagnosis.

81
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.840
Tasmania cannot cut its way to prosperity
while asking less

82
00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.200
of its extractive industries than almost
any other state.

83
00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.000
It also requires the Liberals' grounded
accounting.

84
00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.680
That means abandoning inflated single-year
savings claims and accepting that

85
00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.920
new corporate taxes require realistic,
legally tested runways.

86
00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.160
For now, the choice is binary.

87
00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.080
Choosing the liberal path prioritizes
legacy industries at the cost

88
00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.080
of hollowed-out public services.

89
00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:00.760
Choosing the Greens path protects those
public services, but requires

90
00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.440
accepting high financial volatility as you
fight corporate entities for

91
00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:09.080
that revenue. Tasmania's fiscal crisis
persists because the political price

92
00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:12.920
of an honest, long-term solution remains
too high for either

93
00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.360
side to pay.

